---
title: Combining two maps
---
Two maps, each from a pipeline of its own, joined into one: the talk’s point that a map rarely needs just one technique [[t:179-185 s:20]].

## The rule
```text
build the first input on a map of its own
build the second input on a map of its own
the result's left half is the first map's, and its right half the second's
```

The talk’s example is a fortress of rooms on the left that breaks out into caves on the right [[t:181-185]]. Its demo copies the halves column for column and joins nothing [[c09:100-114]]. The talk’s author then adds a prefab of fortifications down the middle [[t:186-188]].

